A||||3||L.I. Fieros||NOTICE: Bent Suspension Bolts!!! ---- Anyone Else???||||4||
Z||000000||L.I. Fieros||12-09-2000||06:37 PM||||NOTICE: Upon removing the bolt that holds the rear knuckle of my 86 SE to the lower ball joint, I discovered that it was bent/distorted.  This bolt is locked in position to the lower ball joint through the use of a groove on the ball joint shaft.  Has anyone else noticed this bolt bending?  I am trying to figure out what is causing this bolt to bend.  My car has urethane bushings and a rear sway bar installed.  I had lowering springs on the car, but they were removed after about 8K miles.  The bolt was not loose or over torqued because I use a torque wrench on everything.  Right now, I am thinking that the sway bar is causing this because it is the only thing that would pull down on the control arm.  Without a sway bar the control arm is just along for the ride.  However, if it is the sway bar, then thousands of Fiero owners would have been reporting of bent bolts.  If anyone has removed this bolt (maybe to change ball joints) after driving a Fiero with a sway bar for a while and it has or has not shown any sign of being bent please let me know.  This has me very concerned.  The ony other "suspect" is a bump steer modification to the rear end, which will be looked into if nobody else has had this bolt bend.<P>Thanks for your time/help/input,<BR>See ya,<BR>Dave||||reg||4
Z||000001||strdream||12-09-2000||09:27 PM||||The sway bar gets it energy from the other wheel. I have a hard time believing that could cause it. <BR>The only thing I can think of that causes bent suspension parts is sliding sidways and hitting something hard like a curb.<BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-10-2000||12:02 AM||||could be the wrong grade bolt.||||reg||1
Z||000003||L.I. Fieros||12-10-2000||12:35 PM||||Guess I should have mentioned that I completely rebuilt the suspension about a year ago and everything was fine.  Oh, and the bolt is the factory bolt (10.9 hardness) and was torqued to 37 ft.lbs. according to the spec listed in the Helm Service Manual.  The car has also never been hit.<P>Thanks,<BR>See ya,<BR>Dave||||reg||1
